From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] serialposix: custom baud rates on Linux MIPS

pyserial 3.5 uses the asm-generic TCGETS2/TCSETS2 numbers and writes the
custom speed at termios2 index 9/10 on every Linux machine. MIPS encodes
ioctl directions differently (_IOC_READ 2, _IOC_WRITE 4, 3 dir bits) and
its struct termios2 has NCCS 23, so it is 48 bytes with c_ispeed and
c_ospeed at int index 10 and 11. The asm-generic numbers end in ENOTTY
("[Errno 25] Inappropriate ioctl for device"), so every baud rate that is
not a B* constant, Klipper's default 250000 among them, fails to open.

Backport of the MIPS branch as it stands on pyserial master
(a5c48d445fbc1943d4fabf8d9090a50fda3172fd); pyserial has had no release
after 3.5:
 - 5ce1773fdce16a0b184363695a7d7d9483c4da0c, PR #496 (merge baa7c78a):
   "Add support for setting a custom baudrate on the MIPS platform",
   the MIPS TCGETS2/TCSETS2/BAUDRATE_OFFSET values and
   buf[BAUDRATE_OFFSET] = buf[BAUDRATE_OFFSET + 1]
 - 2aea0ba436d7a6af2f9f81b0daf245946b76dfe3 and
   5fb3bc6b52376289990f47fb4f293a0332363d31, PR #723: the machine test
   becomes platform.machine().startswith('mips')
 - 5eb1eafe1091d38c5478c16ecbb04e6c82d7eb47 (Linux ppc): only its move
   of BOTHER into each branch is taken, with the same value as before;
   the ppc branch itself and its whitespace changes are left out.
The 64-int termios2 buffer is already in 3.5, nothing to take there.

Upstream: https://github.com/pyserial/pyserial/commit/5ce1773fdce16a0b184363695a7d7d9483c4da0c
Upstream: https://github.com/pyserial/pyserial/commit/5fb3bc6b52376289990f47fb4f293a0332363d31
Kiln OS issue: https://github.com/djvalic/kiln-os/issues/59
---
 serial/serialposix.py | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/serial/serialposix.py b/serial/serialposix.py
index 7aceb76..4e9bb7f 100644
--- a/serial/serialposix.py
+++ b/serial/serialposix.py
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ from __future__ import absolute_import
 import errno
 import fcntl
 import os
+import platform
 import select
 import struct
 import sys
@@ -80,9 +81,16 @@ if plat[:5] == 'linux':    # Linux (confirmed)  # noqa
     CMSPAR = 0o10000000000  # Use "stick" (mark/space) parity
 
     # baudrate ioctls
-    TCGETS2 = 0x802C542A
-    TCSETS2 = 0x402C542B
-    BOTHER = 0o010000
+    if platform.machine().startswith('mips'):
+        TCGETS2 = 0x4030542A
+        TCSETS2 = 0x8030542B
+        BAUDRATE_OFFSET = 10
+        BOTHER = 0o010000
+    else:
+        TCGETS2 = 0x802C542A
+        TCSETS2 = 0x402C542B
+        BAUDRATE_OFFSET = 9
+        BOTHER = 0o010000
 
     # RS485 ioctls
     TIOCGRS485 = 0x542E
@@ -154,7 +162,7 @@ if plat[:5] == 'linux':    # Linux (confirmed)  # noqa
                 # set custom speed
                 buf[2] &= ~termios.CBAUD
                 buf[2] |= BOTHER
-                buf[9] = buf[10] = baudrate
+                buf[BAUDRATE_OFFSET] = buf[BAUDRATE_OFFSET + 1] = baudrate
 
                 # set serial_struct
                 fcntl.ioctl(self.fd, TCSETS2, buf)
